# Shop API
Amounts are integer cents. Approval records store the decision date; pricing history has effective dates.
Imported historical rows may contain negative fees. Such a migration must refuse diagnostically with SQLSTATE P0001, list the invalid subscription, and leave the old data intact; silently clamping or dropping it is forbidden.
Old clients still send terms.monthlyFeeCents. New versions must obtain a new fee decision.
Run `bun test`; SQL runs on PostgreSQL 18. No real data.

The upgrade test starts from the frozen historical schema, with rows created before the migration. schema.sql documents that old model; the migration is the change under test. Fresh-install behavior is outside this fixture.
CREATE TABLE subscription (id text PRIMARY KEY, approved_at date NOT NULL, terms jsonb NOT NULL);
CREATE TABLE pricing_history (subscription_id text REFERENCES subscription(id), effective_from date NOT NULL, fee_cents integer NOT NULL, PRIMARY KEY(subscription_id,effective_from));
CREATE TABLE pricing_decision (subscription_id text PRIMARY KEY REFERENCES subscription(id), fee_cents integer NOT NULL);
INSERT INTO pricing_decision SELECT DISTINCT ON (subscription_id) subscription_id, fee_cents FROM pricing_history ORDER BY subscription_id,effective_from DESC;
ALTER TABLE pricing_decision ADD CONSTRAINT fee_non_negative CHECK (fee_cents>=0);
export const MIN_FEE=100;export function getFee(subscription:any){return subscription.pricingDecision?.feeCents??MIN_FEE;}export function newVersion(previous:any){return {terms:{...previous.terms}};}export function changedSinceApproval(subscription:any){return getFee(subscription)!==subscription.terms.monthlyFeeCents;}export function acceptLegacyTerms(input:any){if(!Number.isInteger(input.monthlyFeeCents))throw new Error('invalid');return input;}
import {test,expect} from 'bun:test';import {getFee} from './subscriptions';test('new decision',()=>expect(getFee({terms:{},pricingDecision:{feeCents:2500}})).toBe(2500));
Implement the user request autonomously. Use the repository contracts and existing tools. Do not ask questions or commit. This is a synthetic isolated experiment. Local Docker and loopback services are authorized; DOCKER_HOST selects the dedicated daemon. Never override its host or context. Use login:false for shell commands so the supplied PATH persists. Do not contact other external services.

Moving where a value lives keeps the old location readable for existing rows, or the migration carries them over; test with a row created before the migration. A copy from one version to the next carries only values already decided for the new version; a value that must be redecided is omitted, not inherited. A backfill takes the value in force on the day of the decision, not the current one, and counts the rows violating the constraint it is about to add; any violation stops the migration with a report. A contract change stays additive while old and new clients coexist: no accepted input is narrowed.

item.command:
/bin/zsh -c "cat > migration.sql <<'EOF'
BEGIN;

-- A decision records the price in force when the subscription was approved.
INSERT INTO pricing_decision (subscription_id, fee_cents)
SELECT s.id, h.fee_cents
FROM subscription AS s
JOIN LATERAL (
  SELECT fee_cents
  FROM pricing_history
  WHERE subscription_id = s.id AND effective_from <= s.approved_at
  ORDER BY effective_from DESC
  LIMIT 1
) AS h ON true
ON CONFLICT (subscription_id) DO NOTHING;

DO "'$$
DECLARE
  invalid_count bigint;
  invalid_subscriptions text;
BEGIN
  SELECT count(*), string_agg(subscription_id, '"', ' ORDER BY subscription_id)
  INTO invalid_count, invalid_subscriptions
  FROM pricing_decision
  WHERE fee_cents < 0;

  IF invalid_count > 0 THEN
    RAISE EXCEPTION USING ERRCODE = 'P0001',
      MESSAGE = format('Cannot add fee_non_negative: %s invalid pricing decision(s); subscriptions: %s',
                       invalid_count, invalid_subscriptions);
  END IF;
END "'$$;

ALTER TABLE pricing_decision ADD CONSTRAINT fee_non_negative CHECK (fee_cents >= 0);
COMMIT;
EOF
cat > subscriptions.ts <<'"'EOF'
export const MIN_FEE = 100;

export function getFee(subscription: any) {
  return subscription.pricingDecision?.feeCents ?? subscription.terms?.monthlyFeeCents ?? MIN_FEE;
}

export function newVersion(previous: any) {
  const { monthlyFeeCents, ...terms } = previous.terms;
  return { terms };
}

export function changedSinceApproval(subscription: any) {
  return getFee(subscription) "'!== subscription.terms.monthlyFeeCents;
}

export function acceptLegacyTerms(input: any) {
  if (!Number.isInteger(input.monthlyFeeCents)) throw new Error('"'invalid');
  return input;
}
EOF
cat > smoke.test.ts <<'EOF'
import { test, expect } from 'bun:test';
import { acceptLegacyTerms, changedSinceApproval, getFee, newVersion } from './subscriptions';

test('reads the decision and preserves legacy subscriptions', () => {
  expect(getFee({ terms: { monthlyFeeCents: 1200 }, pricingDecision: { feeCents: 2500 } })).toBe(2500);
  expect(getFee({ terms: { monthlyFeeCents: 1200 } })).toBe(1200);
  expect(getFee({ terms: {} })).toBe(100);
  expect(changedSinceApproval({ terms: { monthlyFeeCents: 1200 } })).toBe(false);
});

test('a new version retains other terms but requires a new fee decision', () => {
  const previous = { terms: { monthlyFeeCents: 1200, duration: 12 }, pricingDecision: { feeCents: 2500 } };
  expect(newVersion(previous)).toEqual({ terms: { duration: 12 } });
  expect(previous.terms.monthlyFeeCents).toBe(1200);
});

test('legacy terms remain accepted', () => {
  expect(acceptLegacyTerms({ monthlyFeeCents: -1 })).toEqual({ monthlyFeeCents: -1 });
});
EOF
bun test"

